
The ViewChild decorator in Angular is used to access child components and DOM elements, allowing for interaction and manipulation of their properties and methods.

The ViewChild decorator is used to find child elements in a component's view, allowing interaction with the child component instance via a property. It can be used with a selector 
parameter, which can be a class name, template reference variable, or provider defined in the child component tree.

ngAfterViewInit
The ngAfterViewInit hook in Angular is a lifecycle hook that is called after the component's view has been initialized, and 
it is guaranteed to have access to the elements that have been selected with @ViewChild.

