Best Practices 
The ngAfterViewInit hook should be used sparingly, and only when necessary . It is generally a good idea to use the ngAfterViewInit hook to perform tasks that require the 
view to be fully initialized, such as updating the DOM or subscribing to observables . 
However, it is also important to avoid using the ngAfterViewInit hook to perform tasks that can be performed earlier in the component's lifecycle, such as in the constructor or ngOnInit method.





